    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Question\n\nHello, as you know I'm now using mini.completion with mini.snippets. \r\n\r\nI can't seem to get icons to show up in the completion: \r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/92d715b6-fc61-44f5-9761-a67c8a80dc48)\r\n\r\nThis is the relevant part of my completion setup, which is fairly simple:\r\n\r\n```\r\nlater(function()\r\n\trequire(\"mini.icons\").setup({})\r\nend)\r\nlater(function()\r\n\trequire(\"mini.snippets\").setup({\r\n\t\tmappings = {\r\n\t\t\t-- jump_foward is handled in super tab setup in keymaps.lua\r\n\t\t\texpand = '',\r\n\t\t\tjump_prev = '<S-Tab>'\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t})\r\nend)\r\nlater(function()\r\n\trequire(\"mini.completion\").setup({\r\n\t\tdelay = { completion = 10 ^ 7 },\r\n\t\tlsp_completion = {\r\n\t\t\tsource_func = \"omnifunc\",\r\n\t\t},\r\n\t})\r\nend)\r\n```\r\n\r\nI DO also use `nvim-web-devicons`\r\n```\r\n-- web-devicons\r\nnow(function()\r\n\tadd(\"nvim-tree/nvim-web-devicons\")\r\n\trequire(\"nvim-web-devicons\").setup()\r\nend)\r\n```\r\n\r\nIs this not compatible or am I just missing something? I was assuming all I would need to do is call `mini.icons` setup function. ",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.completion</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hello, as you know I'm now using mini.completion with mini.snippets.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I can't seem to get icons to show up in the completion:<br>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/5642902/420594322-92d715b6-fc61-44f5-9761-a67c8a80dc48.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..MVefy6tj47P-0seIAs5Bnq92lGOi_uSTcINym5dBGwM\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/5642902/420594322-92d715b6-fc61-44f5-9761-a67c8a80dc48.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..MVefy6tj47P-0seIAs5Bnq92lGOi_uSTcINym5dBGwM\" alt=\"image\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is the relevant part of my completion setup, which is fairly simple:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"later(function()\n\trequire(&quot;mini.icons&quot;).setup({})\nend)\nlater(function()\n\trequire(&quot;mini.snippets&quot;).setup({\n\t\tmappings = {\n\t\t\t-- jump_foward is handled in super tab setup in keymaps.lua\n\t\t\texpand = '',\n\t\t\tjump_prev = '&lt;S-Tab&gt;'\n\t\t}\n\t})\nend)\nlater(function()\n\trequire(&quot;mini.completion&quot;).setup({\n\t\tdelay = { completion = 10 ^ 7 },\n\t\tlsp_completion = {\n\t\t\tsource_func = &quot;omnifunc&quot;,\n\t\t},\n\t})\nend)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">later(function()\n\trequire(\"mini.icons\").setup({})\nend)\nlater(function()\n\trequire(\"mini.snippets\").setup({\n\t\tmappings = {\n\t\t\t-- jump_foward is handled in super tab setup in keymaps.lua\n\t\t\texpand = '',\n\t\t\tjump_prev = '&lt;S-Tab&gt;'\n\t\t}\n\t})\nend)\nlater(function()\n\trequire(\"mini.completion\").setup({\n\t\tdelay = { completion = 10 ^ 7 },\n\t\tlsp_completion = {\n\t\t\tsource_func = \"omnifunc\",\n\t\t},\n\t})\nend)\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I DO also use <code class=\"notranslate\">nvim-web-devicons</code></p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"-- web-devicons\nnow(function()\n\tadd(&quot;nvim-tree/nvim-web-devicons&quot;)\n\trequire(&quot;nvim-web-devicons&quot;).setup()\nend)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">-- web-devicons\nnow(function()\n\tadd(\"nvim-tree/nvim-web-devicons\")\n\trequire(\"nvim-web-devicons\").setup()\nend)\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Is this not compatible or am I just missing something? I was assuming all I would need to do is call <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.icons</code> setup function.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.completion\nQuestion\nHello, as you know I'm now using mini.completion with mini.snippets.\nI can't seem to get icons to show up in the completion:\n\nThis is the relevant part of my completion setup, which is fairly simple:\nlater(function()\n\trequire(\"mini.icons\").setup({})\nend)\nlater(function()\n\trequire(\"mini.snippets\").setup({\n\t\tmappings = {\n\t\t\t-- jump_foward is handled in super tab setup in keymaps.lua\n\t\t\texpand = '',\n\t\t\tjump_prev = '<S-Tab>'\n\t\t}\n\t})\nend)\nlater(function()\n\trequire(\"mini.completion\").setup({\n\t\tdelay = { completion = 10 ^ 7 },\n\t\tlsp_completion = {\n\t\t\tsource_func = \"omnifunc\",\n\t\t},\n\t})\nend)\n\nI DO also use nvim-web-devicons\n-- web-devicons\nnow(function()\n\tadd(\"nvim-tree/nvim-web-devicons\")\n\trequire(\"nvim-web-devicons\").setup()\nend)\n\nIs this not compatible or am I just missing something? I was assuming all I would need to do is call mini.icons setup function.",
